#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
repo_root="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
while IFS=$'\t' read -r setting app state; do
  [[ -n "$setting" && "$setting" != \#* ]] || continue
  printf "  %s: %s = %s\n" "$setting" "$app" "$state"
done < "$repo_root/apps/obs-permissions.tsv"
cat <<'EOF'

After OBS is installed, open OBS and use its permissions dialog:
  Screen Recording: open preferences and enable OBS.
  Camera and Microphone: click Request Access for each, then allow access.
  Input Monitoring: open preferences and enable OBS for background hotkeys.
If OBS is missing from a settings list, request access from OBS first.
On older installations, OBS may use Accessibility instead of Input Monitoring;
use that entry only if OBS directs you there. Reopen the permissions dialog
from the OBS Studio menu if needed. Restart OBS when macOS requests it.
EOF
